---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Terminal from '../../components/Terminal.astro';

const description =
  'Install the CLI, stamp the factory into a repo, and prove the whole path with a read-only run.';
---
<DocsLayout
  title="Quickstart"
  description={description}
  current="/docs/quickstart"
  prev={{ href: '/docs/', label: 'Overview' }}
  next={{ href: '/docs/core-concepts', label: 'Core concepts' }}
>
  <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Tool</th><th>Why</th><th>Checked by</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="cmd">uv</span> + Python 3.11+</td><td>The CLI is installed as a uv tool</td><td><span class="cmd">sssf doctor</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="cmd">pi</span></td><td>The coding agent every agent phase runs</td><td><span class="cmd">sssf doctor</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="cmd">bun</span></td><td>Serves the global visualizer (<span class="cmd">sssf viz</span>)</td><td><span class="cmd">sssf doctor</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="cmd">sqlite3</span></td><td>The trace database reads</td><td><span class="cmd">sssf doctor</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="cmd">docker</span></td><td>Sandboxed runs (optional for local runs)</td><td><span class="cmd">sssf sandbox build</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    You also need a model registered in the coding agent&rsquo;s catalog for whatever
    <code class="hl">model:</code> entries your roster names. <span class="cmd">sssf doctor</span>
    checks the toolchain; a missing API key fails when that agent runs, not at startup.
  </p>

  <h2>1 · Install</h2>
  <pre><code>uv tool install sssf</code></pre>
  <p>
    One global install, any number of projects. You can also install from a checkout with
    <code class="hl">uv tool install --editable .</code>. There is no per-project install step:
    that is what <span class="cmd">sssf init</span> is for.
  </p>

  <h2>2 · Stamp the factory into a repo</h2>
  <pre><code>cd your-repo
sssf init</code></pre>
  <p>
    <span class="cmd">sssf init</span> stamps the <strong>customization surface</strong> into the
    current directory and registers the project:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code class="hl">adws/modules/adw_*.py</code>: your chains (AI Developer Workflows)</li>
    <li><code class="hl">adws/config/sssf.config.yaml</code>: your agent roster</li>
    <li><code class="hl">adws/data/prompt_engineering/</code>: your prompts, per agent</li>
    <li><code class="hl">adws/data/harness_engineering/</code>: pi extensions</li>
    <li><code class="hl">.env.sample</code>: provider keys template</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    It also appends an <code class="hl">&lt;!-- sssf --&gt;</code> block to
    <code class="hl">AGENTS.md</code> and adds the runtime state
    (<code class="hl">adws/data/sessions/</code>, <code class="hl">sssf.db</code> and its WAL
    sidecars) to <code class="hl">.gitignore</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>3 · Run something safe</h2>
  <pre><code>sssf run scout "map the repo"</code></pre>
  <p>
    <span class="cmd">scout</span> is the read-only recon chain: it changes nothing. A green run
    proves the whole path end to end: config validated, session minted, agent ran, envelope
    parsed, events landed in <code class="hl">adws/data/sssf.db</code>. Fix it here before
    composing anything larger, because every multi-agent chain rides this exact path.
  </p>
  <p>
    Want to see it before wiring your own project? The
    <a href="https://github.com/felipemm/inkwell">inkwell</a> demo repo is ready to run —
    clone it and run <code>sssf run</code> to watch a full traced chain.
  </p>
  <p>
    The <code class="hl">adw_</code> prefix is optional: <span class="cmd">sssf run adw_scout</span>
    and <span class="cmd">sssf run scout</span> are the same thing.
  </p>

  <h2>4 · Look at the trace</h2>
  <pre><code>sssf sessions        # recent runs, status, tokens, cost
sssf phases a1b2c3d4  # the phase waterfall of one run
sssf tail a1b2c3d4    # recent events of one run
sssf procs a1b2c3d4   # live processes of one run</code></pre>

  <h2>5 · Open the visualizer</h2>
  <pre><code>sssf viz</code></pre>
  <p>
    Spawns the global visualizer as a background service on port <code class="hl">4600</code> and
    opens your browser. It is a global service over every registered project, with a project
    picker in the UI. If the healer is not running, <span class="cmd">sssf viz start</span> rides
    it along.
  </p>
  <div style="margin-top: 26px;">
    <Terminal
      title="sssf: the whole quickstart"
      lines={[
        { kind: 'prompt', text: '❯ uv tool install sssf' },
        { kind: 'out', text: '✓ installed sssf 1.0.0' },
        { kind: 'prompt', text: '❯ sssf init' },
        { kind: 'out', text: '✓ stamped adws/ · registered <repo>' },
        { kind: 'prompt', text: '❯ sssf run scout "map the repo"' },
        { kind: 'ok', text: '✔ scout done: findings in context_handoff/' },
        { kind: 'prompt', text: '❯ sssf sessions' },
        { kind: 'out', text: 'a1b2c3d4  scout  success  3 findings  1.4k tok  $0.00' },
        { kind: 'prompt', text: '❯ sssf viz' },
        { kind: 'out', text: '→ http://localhost:4600/#/status' },
      ]}
    />
  </div>

  <h2>Sanity check</h2>
  <pre><code>sssf doctor   # uv · pi · bun · sqlite3 · ~/.local/bin on PATH</code></pre>
  <p>
    <span class="cmd">sssf doctor</span> checks the global prerequisites and reports each one
    with the path it resolved. Every recipe here is also available as a plain command: nothing
    depends on aliases or wrappers.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
